# Infrastructure Conventions

## Docker Services

All services run in Docker Compose on the `toro-net` network:

| Service | Port | Purpose |
|---------|------|---------|
| gate | 8080 | Webhook ingress (REST) |
| graphql | 8082 | GraphQL API |
| ws | 8081 | WebSocket server |
| sync | — | QBO/Plaid background sync |
| cdc-worker | — | Change Data Capture |
| protocol | — | Agent protocol service |
| python-worker | — | Python NATS subscriber |
| nginx | 80 | Reverse proxy |
| db | 5435 | PostgreSQL (TimescaleDB) |
| redis | 6380 | Cache + token blacklist |
| nats-1/2/3 | — | JetStream cluster |

## Docker Compose

- `container/docker-compose.yml` — development
- `container/docker-compose.prod.yml` — production overrides
- `ENVIRONMENT` determined by `PRODUCTION_SERVER` env var

## Build & Deploy

- `make build` — build all service images
- `make up` — start dev stack (creates `toro-net` if missing)
- `make deploy` — git-based deployment trigger
- Each service has its own `container/<service>/Dockerfile`

## Configuration

- Viper reads `defaults.yaml` + environment variable overrides
- Config struct validated at startup — fail fast on invalid config
- Secrets (encryption keys, JWT keys) via env vars, never committed
- Connection pool sizes, timeouts, and limits are configurable

## Health Checks

- `GET /health/live` — liveness probe (process running)
- `GET /health/ready` — readiness probe (DB + NATS reachable)
